A few things to notice:
- Every trajectory is pulled toward the **periodic attracting solution** that wiggles around $y=0$ — the unique bounded solution as $x\to\infty$.
- The homogeneous part $\dot y=-y$ kills transients exponentially; $\sin(x)$ injects the steady oscillation.
- Closed form: $y(x)=\tfrac12(\sin x - \cos x) + Ce^{-x}$. The $Ce^{-x}$ term is the transient you see decaying.

